      "archive_timestamp": "20250207183431",
      "article_id": "article_3a4618cd5c1c35ab",
      "body_recovery_method": "wayback",
      "context_excerpt": "Using NVIDIA Ampere and L40 GPUs , the Baker Lab used its deep learning models, including RFdiffusion and ProteinMPNN, to generate millions of potential antitoxin structures ‘in silico,’ or in computer simulations. Instead of screening a vast number of these proteins in a lab, they used AI tools to predict how the designer proteins would interact with snake venom toxins, rapidly homing in on the most promising designs.",
